@startuml domain-registration
' Report §2.4 — Registration bounded context in full. The classes come from
' include/domain-registration.iuml, the same source the overview (domain-model.puml) uses.
!pragma layout smetana
!include include/style.iuml
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty members

title Registration context (registration-service) — domain model

!include include/domain-registration.iuml
!include include/domain-published-language.iuml
!$only = "registration"
!include include/domain-event-links.iuml

remove @unlinked
hide <<DomainEvent>> members

note top of Registration
  <b>Invariants</b>
  · holds seats for at least one session
  · a total above zero needs a card token
    (it travels on registration-requested
    and is never stored)
  · a zero total is confirmed at once and
    never emits registration-requested
  · confirm / cancel / expire only from
    PENDING_PAYMENT
end note

note bottom of SessionView
  Local replica of catalogue data, fed by
  session-added and session-capacity-changed,
  so seat allocation never calls the catalogue.
  reservedSeats is maintained here. @Version
  serialises concurrent reservations.
  isComplete() is false until session-added
  has arrived (capacity may arrive first).
end note

note bottom of SeatAllocationService
  Checks every requested session before
  creating any hold: one full session
  refuses the whole registration (409
  SESSION_FULL). Holds expire at
  now + HoldWindow (PT2M demo default).
end note

legend right
  Value objects are Java records; AttendeeRef, Money
  and TimeSlot are JPA @Embeddable. HoldWindow is
  configuration (conference.registration.hold-window).
  Money is duplicated in Billing on purpose.
  RegistrationStatus.REFUNDED exists, but no use
  case on main sets it (FR-11).
endlegend
@enduml
